+# Due Date Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Todos bekommen ein optionales Fälligkeitsdatum (`YYYY-MM-DD`); API und Liste zeigen überfällige Todos an, API filtert per `?overdue=true`, Liste hat einen `nur überfällige`-Button.
+
+**Architecture:** `dueDate` als optionales Feld (`string | null`) im Todo-Objekt, validiert in `src/store.mjs` (bestehendes ValidationError-Muster). Der API-Filter `GET /todos?overdue=true` wird in `src/app.mjs` umgesetzt (store.list() bleibt unverändert). Die UI in `public/index.html` rendert `fällig: <datum>` und `überfällig` clientseitig und toggelt per Button. Überfällig-Logik überall: `!done && dueDate !== null && dueDate < heute (UTC, YYYY-MM-DD)`.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Node 24 builtins only (`node:http`, `node:test`), zero dependencies, clientseitiges Vanilla-JS in `public/index.html`.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-23-due-date-design.md`
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Zero dependencies — Node builtins only.
+- Validation errors are `ValidationError` from `src/store.mjs` and map to HTTP 400.
+- TDD: write a failing test in `test/` first.
+- UI elements tests rely on carry a `data-testid` (existing: `todo-list`, `todo-item`, `todo-title`; new: `todo-due`, `todo-overdue`, `filter-overdue`).
+- `dueDate` format: `YYYY-MM-DD` only, validated as a real calendar date.
+- Overdue: `!done && dueDate !== null && dueDate < today`, `today = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)` (UTC). String comparison is sufficient for `YYYY-MM-DD`.
+- No styling for overdue todos — the word `überfällig` is the only marker.
+- E2E: agent tests in the running app via Playwright (AGENTS.md end-to-end section).
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- Invalid `dueDate` values (wrong format, impossible date like `2026-02-30`, wrong type) must yield HTTP 400, not 500 — pinned in Task 1 tests.
+- `dueDate: null` in PATCH must clear the date; a todo without a date is never overdue — pinned in Tasks 1 and 2 tests.
+- Boundary: a todo due *today* is not overdue; a done todo with a past date is not overdue — pinned in Task 2 tests.
+- `GET /todos` without query params must stay byte-identical in behavior (all todos, unchanged shape plus `dueDate: null`) — pinned in Task 2 tests.
+- UI filter button must toggle both ways without a refetch, and overdue marking must use UTC today — exercised in the E2E step of Task 3.
+
+---
+
